WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.500
UMAP.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:06.633
Like t-SNE, but faster, and the best tool for looking inside an embedding space.

3
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:09.900
UMAP plays the same game as t-SNE.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.300
It projects non-linearly, keeping local neighborhoods, but it also preserves more of the global structure.

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.333
And it can transform new points, which t-SNE classically cannot.

6
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:22.667
How does it compare?

7
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:27.067
UMAP is much faster, and scales to hundreds of thousands of points.

8
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:32.600
The relative placement of islands is somewhat more meaningful, though still not literal distance.

9
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.400
Better, but not perfect.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.900
Here is the killer app for an AI engineer.

11
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.967
Take your text, headlines or document chunks.

12
00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.733
Embed them into high dimensional vectors.

13
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.600
Project them to two dimensions with UMAP.

14
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:47.552
Then look.

15
00:00:47.552 --> 00:00:49.442
Do topics form clean islands?

16
00:00:49.442 --> 00:00:51.267
Where do duplicates pile up?

17
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:53.800
Two knobs matter most.

18
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.433
N neighbors: small values show local detail, large values show the global shape.

19
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:02.300
And min dist controls how tightly points pack.

20
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.033
In code, we embed first.

21
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:10.433
Two hundred space news headlines become three hundred eighty four dimensional embeddings.

22
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:14.600
Then UMAP projects them to two dimensions, and we scatter the result.

23
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.400
Here is a debugging story.

24
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.233
Mission Control RAG keeps retrieving irrelevant chunks for propulsion queries.

25
00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:28.000
You UMAP the vector store, and propulsion and electrical power are fused into one island.

26
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.001
The chunking split documents mid section.

27
00:01:31.001 --> 00:01:33.833
Re-chunk, re-embed, and retrieval improves.

28
00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:35.839
Let's recap.

29
00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:39.600
UMAP is faster than t-SNE, with better global structure.

30
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.467
It can transform new points.

31
00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.533
Use it to eyeball your embeddings.

32
00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:45.333
Next up: accuracy.
